preConditionHook:
// RATCHET THE STOP BEHIND THE LAST STRONG TREND BAR. Each time a bar closes as
// a strong with-trend bar, the protective level moves to just beyond that bar's
// NEAR extreme -- the low for a long, the high for a short -- and it only ever
// moves TOWARD the trade. Through a run of weak bars it does not move at all,
// which is what separates it from the dollar trails.
//
// Not TrailingStop / AtrTrailingStop, which measure a distance below the
// position's PEAK PROFIT: this is a chart level pinned to a particular bar and
// can sit far from the peak. Not TightenStopToEntryBarIfStrong, which tests the
// ENTRY bar once and afterwards never moves.
//
// THE LEVEL IS PER POSITION and is cleared on ctx.BarsSinceEntry() == 0 --
// VERIFIED as 0 on the fill bar and as restarting through a reversal, which a
// ctx.MarketPosition() == 0 reset would miss because a reversal never passes
// through flat. While flat the clear simply repeats. The fill bar itself can
// seed the level, and a bar can never take itself out: the seed is that bar's
// own low minus an offset, and close >= low always.
//
// THE RATCHET IS WRITTEN AS AN if, NOT MaxList: the register ACCEPTS MaxList
// only for tick-grid price operands, and a seeded-or-not level needs the flag
// test anyway.
//
// "Strong" is the body-fraction test, body >= strongBodyFraction of the bar's
// own range, as StrongTrendBarRun writes it. The comparison is a MULTIPLICATION,
// never a division, so a zero-range bar cannot raise EL's divide-by-zero.
// R01-02's alternative reading defines strong by RANGE against an ATR; the body
// test wins because it needs no ATR call site.
//
// Ticks: MinMove/PriceScale are VERIFIED and the tick is written division-first,
// stopOffsetTicks * (ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale()), computed once per bar
// into a local because the two are per-symbol constants for the whole run.
//
// Every scratch value is a localVariables entry, never a hook-scope
// declaration, so the hooks survive a double placement.
//
// Deepest bar touched: 0.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
if (ctx.BarsSinceEntry() == 0) {
    haveTrailLong = false;
    haveTrailShort = false;
    trailLong = 0.0;
    trailShort = 0.0;
}
barRange = high[0] - low[0];
bodySize = close[0] - open[0];
strongBull = el_gt(close[0], open[0]) && el_ge(bodySize, strongBodyFraction * barRange);
strongBear = el_lt(close[0], open[0]) && el_ge(-bodySize, strongBodyFraction * barRange);
if (strongBull) {
    candLevel = low[0] - stopOffsetTicks * tickSize;
    if (!haveTrailLong || el_gt(candLevel, trailLong)) {
        trailLong = candLevel;
        haveTrailLong = true;
    }
}
if (strongBear) {
    candLevel = high[0] + stopOffsetTicks * tickSize;
    if (!haveTrailShort || el_lt(candLevel, trailShort)) {
        trailShort = candLevel;
        haveTrailShort = true;
    }
}
